   "reasoning_summary": "C20H18O6 has DoU 12, consistent with a prenylated flavonoid: chromone (C15) + C5 prenyl + 4 OH. The chelated 5-OH at 13.00 and C=O at 182.0 indicate a 5-hydroxychromone. Meta A-ring protons at 6.43/6.29 sit on C 94.5/99.8, indicating 5,7-dioxygenation. The singlet at 7.89 on a CH at 155.2 suggests isoflavone H-2. Catechol carbons at 145.6/144.2 and two B-ring protons at 6.76/6.56 suggest a 2'-prenyl-4',5'-dihydroxy B ring. Prenyl signals appear at 5.08, 3.30, 1.52 and 1.43. Seventeen of the 18 H are listed, with three OH unlisted. There are 19 13C signals for 20 carbons, so one is overlapped or missing. Alternatives are a 3-prenylflavone and licoisoflavone A."
